%% Figure: Rebooking a disrupted passenger (UC4) - the AI proposes, the database decides
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P as Passenger
    participant W as Kestrel Web
    participant A as Assistant (Gemini + tools)
    participant R as REST tier
    participant D as Postgres

    P->>W: Sign in (booking ref + surname)
    W->>R: POST /api/auth/guest
    R->>D: look up booking
    R-->>W: signed session token
    W->>R: GET /api/trip (token)
    R->>D: booking, cancelled flight, same-route alternatives
    R-->>W: trip + recommended flight
    P->>A: "Rebook me on the next flight"
    A->>R: find_alternative_flights_tool (token)
    R-->>A: same-route flights with free seats
    A-->>P: proposes KQ608, asks to confirm
    P->>W: Confirm rebooking
    W->>R: POST /api/reaccommodate (token, flight)
    R->>D: CALL reaccommodate_passenger_atomic
    Note over D: lock booking FOR UPDATE<br/>check same route and departure in future<br/>pick seat FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED<br/>update booking + seat, write audit row
    alt seat assigned
        D-->>R: REACCOMMODATED, seat 4A
        R->>D: issue vouchers from entitlement rules
        R-->>W: 200 rebooked + vouchers
    else refused (DIFFERENT_ROUTE / no seat / departed)
        D-->>R: refusal code, nothing written
        R->>D: open hand-off case
        R-->>W: 409 + hand-off to staff
    end
    W-->>P: confirmation screen
